{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/515633-what-of-a-skin-lands-stretch-goal-book","id":515633,"title":"What of a Skin Lands Stretch Goal Book?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-15T17:45:30-07:00","id":515633,"title":"What of a Skin Lands Stretch Goal Book?","content":"In all honesty, the greatest part of the tragic tale unfolds when a soul is grasping at life's breath, refusing to be set free from the bonds of the body. Death come, only, unbeknown to the departed, who continues to view life still enduring the the shadows -- when a wraith believes he/she is yet alive, as the body expired, yet sensation &amp; mind tells them otherwise -- a wraith who instead of passing life visions, rather, had an on going reverie, that he/she saw him/herself recover from the grip of death's hand, and now, goes on believing he/she is still alive -- denying the reality of their situation.<br /> <br /> Some have said, ney on the Skin Lands, or cover it loosely. My suggestion is, if not covered in full in the core book, a stretch goal book release that would deal with the Skin Lands would be a nice supplemental addition -- in it, mechanics for a broader based cross over system with the other World of Darkness 20: Settings could manage things out more smoothly. This way, those who may just want a scratch reference, to implement some aspects of the Skin Lands in their Wraith game, could use the Core book as a base referral -- whereas, those who want a more gauging experience, could get a more in depth glance at the &quot;Other Side&quot;, which would serve all systems well, and maybe even help those who have shunned Wraith in the past due to its solidarity, to take another look.<br /> <br /> So, if you ask me what I want, it is just that;<br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#2F4F4F\"><b>Wraith 20: the Skin Lands</b></span>&quot;<br /> <br /> .<br /> .<br /> .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6040-quiet-storm","name":"Quiet Storm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6040_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T01:15:27-07:00","id":515924,"title":"","content":"...The kickstarter is over.<br /> I'm not saying that a Wr20 book on the Skinlands wouldn't be interesting (though I'd tie that into Nercopoli as well), just that it is a little late to come up with 'Stretch Goal release'. Though I can see a small pdf booklet being entertained.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T08:04:11-07:00","id":516193,"title":"","content":"&quot;Things To Do In The Underworld When You're Alive.&quot;<br /> <br /> #1: Run.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T08:35:35-07:00","id":516213,"title":"","content":"#2: ask for number 